      'Drug discovery is the earliest phase of pharmaceutical development, spanning the identification of an unmet medical need through the nomination of a preclinical candidate ready for formal safety testing. It is also the highest-attrition stage of the entire pipeline: of the thousands of molecules screened against a given target, only a small handful ever reach a clinic, and the overall process from initial target hypothesis to an approved medicine typically spans ten to fifteen years and costs well over a billion dollars when failures across the portfolio are accounted for.',
