      'ADME/Tox profiling — Absorption, Distribution, Metabolism, Excretion, and Toxicity — runs in parallel with potency optimization, since a molecule that binds its target perfectly is useless if it cannot reach that target safely inside the body. In vitro assays assess microsomal metabolic stability, Caco-2 cell permeability as a surrogate for intestinal absorption, plasma protein binding, and inhibition of cytochrome P450 enzymes that could cause drug-drug interactions, while early in vivo pharmacokinetic studies in animals characterize how a compound is actually absorbed and cleared.',
