      'Clinical development is organized into a sequence of phases, each designed to answer a specific question and build on the evidence generated by the phase before it, rather than as a single monolithic testing process. This phased structure exists because testing an unproven candidate in large numbers of patients before its basic safety profile is understood would be both unethical and scientifically inefficient, so risk and trial size increase only as confidence in the candidate grows.',
