      'Phase III trials are the large, pivotal, adequately powered randomized controlled trials that provide the primary evidence supporting a marketing application, typically enrolling from several hundred to several thousand patients across multiple sites and often multiple countries. These trials are designed with rigorous statistical pre-specification to distinguish a true treatment effect from chance, and success requires demonstrating not just statistical significance but a clinically meaningful benefit that regulators and physicians agree matters to patients.',
