      'Pharmacogenomics examines how an individual\'s genetic makeup influences their response to medications — both how effectively a drug works and how likely it is to cause an adverse reaction — with the goal of moving away from one-size-fits-all dosing toward genotype-guided, personalized prescribing. The field draws on decades of accumulated evidence that a meaningful share of variability in drug response, long attributed to unexplained individual differences, is in fact predictable from specific, well-characterized genetic variants.',
